# Trivy ignore file — read by default by the CI image scan (aquasecurity/trivy-action).
#
# The entries below are vulnerabilities in Go modules compiled into the
# FrankenPHP binary shipped by the `dunglas/frankenphp:1-php8.4` base image
# (see Dockerfile). They are NOT application dependencies and cannot be fixed
# from this repository via composer/npm — the fix is a base-image update, which
# is picked up automatically once `dunglas/frankenphp` publishes a patched
# `1-php8.4` image (CI builds with `--pull`). They affect `main` identically.
#
# All of them live in FrankenPHP/Caddy surfaces Marketix does not use
# (OpenAPI validation, gRPC/xDS, SSH) — FrankenPHP runs only as the Octane app
# server. Accepted as a documented, temporary exception — re-check and remove
# once the base image is rebuilt.
#
# Entries carry an `exp:` date so CI fails again once it passes and forces a
# re-check instead of silently ignoring them forever.

# github.com/getkin/kin-openapi — ValidationHandler.Load() fail-open auth bypass
# (fixed upstream in 0.144.0; present in the base image's frankenphp binary)
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw

# google.golang.org/grpc — xDS RBAC and HTTP/2 vulnerabilities
# (fixed upstream in 1.82.1; present in the base image's frankenphp binary)
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf

# github.com/getkin/kin-openapi v0.140.0 — DoS via malformed multipart/form-data
# body (fixed in 0.141.0) and via deepObject query parsing (fixed in 0.142.0).
# Upstream FrankenPHP main already ships 0.146.0; not yet released (v1.12.7).
CVE-2026-76905 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-77354 exp:2026-10-31

# golang.org/x/crypto v0.54.0 — x/crypto/ssh auth bypass via unenforced
# source-address restrictions (fixed in 0.55.0). No SSH server in the image.
CVE-2026-56854 exp:2026-10-31

# google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.1 — gRPC-Go vulnerability (fixed in 1.83.1) and
# xDS server DoS (fixed in 1.82.2 / 1.83.2). Still 1.81.1 on FrankenPHP main.
CVE-2026-84304 exp:2026-10-31
CVE-2026-84445 exp:2026-10-31
